                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7134a1f-a428-42e0-921d-b644403349b9",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f5899e1-76fc-3c6f-adba-47c4b60f1450",
                        "source_sense_id": "4bae83b2-fce2-33ad-a4cc-4d9ceb8e8a86",
                        "target_lang_word": "moustache",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "moustache",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                        "entry_id": "142a3941-b993-320b-ad20-233a6378e4f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A growth of facial hair between the nose and the upper lip."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b915e75d-7b10-4c3e-9589-9a7f3fec5d53",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "A moment later there entered a tall thin Englishman with a great moustache, which was a rare thing amid that clean-shaven race."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "269f33ae-0313-47bd-953d-257531531284",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "“A tight little craft,” was Austin’s invariable comment on the matron;[…]. ¶ Near her wandered her husband, orientally bland, invariably affable, and from time to time squinting sideways, as usual, in the ever-renewed expectation that he might catch a glimpse of his stiff, retroussé moustache."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bda21e7-0a7c-4b31-af1e-7a896f5945de",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "A hint of the truth broke on him after Sedan, when he saw the dyed moustaches of Napoleon going grey; another when he entered Paris, and saw the smashed windows of the Tuileries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53d147d5-d9ad-446b-98ee-0ec12b675310",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "Ivan, the confidential man with the scar and the moustaches, came out of the house like a cannon ball, and came racing across the lawn to Valentin like a dog to his master."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec102880-b28e-4a78-baf8-98b1b9d3ab61",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "Small, well-knit, fair, he sat stroking his slight blond moustache and looking at her with kindly, almost tender eyes; but he left it to his sister and the others to draw her out and fit her into the pattern."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c47d626-2e3a-4ab2-a6a8-baec01b36124",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "Crabbe caught the eye of the oboist, an ancient man with dignified moustaches, and mimed that they were going round to the front, to watch the real thing, the shadows."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4afed00-175b-493c-9b15-68911d086dbf",
                                                "sense_id": "acde756e-2a65-30f9-93ae-0086a7728d6d",
                                                "text": "The Stan Lee fly, or Daptolestes leei, which is said to share his characteristic sunglasses and white moustache"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a466d1d-5095-3106-9a95-f20457ff0b36",
